      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We want to find the maximum possible area of an equilateral triangle that can fit within a rectangle with length $10$ and width $11$. \n\nFirst, consider the equilateral triangle with side length $s$. We can draw in the altitude of the triangle, which will split the equilateral triangle into two 30-60-90 right triangles. In a 30-60-90 triangle, the longer leg is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the shorter leg $\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)$ and the hypotenuse is $s$. The altitude of the equilateral triangle is the longer leg of these right triangles, which is $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2}$.\n\nTo fit the equilateral triangle within the rectangle, the triangle must be contained within both the length and the width of the rectangle. Therefore, the altitude of the triangle must be less than or equal to both $\\frac{10}{2} = 5$ and $\\frac{11}{2} = 5.5$. Thus, we have $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\leq 5$ and $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\leq 5.5$.\n\nSolving the first inequality $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\leq 5$ yields:\n\\[s\\sqrt{3} \\leq 10\\]\n\\[s \\leq \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\n\nSolving the second inequality $\\frac{s\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\leq 5.5$ yields:\n\\[s\\sqrt{3} \\leq 11\\]\n\\[s \\leq \\frac{11}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\]\n\nTo find the maximum possible side length of the equilateral triangle, we need to take the maximum of the two results, $\\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ and $\\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3}$. Since $\\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3} > \\frac{10\\sqrt{3}}{3}$, the maximum possible side length is $\\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3}$.\n\nThe area of an equilateral triangle with side length $s$ is given by the formula:\n\\[\\text{Area} = \\frac{s^2 \\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\]\n\nSubstituting $s = \\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ into the formula, we get:\n\\[\\text{Area} = \\frac{\\left(\\frac{11\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right)^2 \\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{\\frac{121 \\cdot 3}{9} \\sqrt{3}}{4} = \\frac{121 \\cdot \\sqrt{3}}{12}.\\]\n\nSo the maximum possible area of the equilateral triangle is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{121\\sqrt{3}}{12}}\\).",
